  "interpretation": "The original 48 sizes end at 112. With 16 simultaneous requests, MTP8 can require 16*(8+1)=144 decode tokens and the backend warns that 112 may be suboptimal. Adding only 117/126/135/144 removes the warning and raises one full-run throughput from 233.61 to 791.13 output token/s. This is strong evidence of insufficient graph coverage, not direct per-step proof of eager fallback. MTP4 has only one new 48-size run, so no median is reported."
